Bi-Lipschitz Factor Flows — provenance and credits

This compact implementation was adapted from the author's local BLAE-main
research workspace. The original workspace carries the following notice,
which is preserved in LICENSE:

    Copyright (c) 2026 qipengz
    MIT License

The MLP encoder structure originates from that workspace's BLAE foundation.
The source map in docs/scope.md records the research components used to build
the public flow model, losses, data generator and evaluation code.

Related work: Qipeng Zhan, Zhuoping Zhou, Zexuan Wang, Qi Long and Li Shen,
"Bi-Lipschitz Autoencoder with Injectivity Guarantee", ICLR 2026, as cited
in the supplied BFF manuscript.

Research manuscript: "Bi-Lipschitz Factor Flows: Regularizing the Latent
Geometry of Flow-Matching Decoders", supplied by the project author.
docs/paper.pdf is an unchanged copy of that manuscript. Its anonymous author
block is retained, and no acceptance status is inferred.

assets/paper_latent_images.png is extracted from Figure 3 of the manuscript.
assets/architecture.png is an explanatory diagram of the public model.
assets/cancellation.png is generated by examples/cancellation.py.
Paper figures and numerical results are labeled separately from outputs of
the public example configurations.

